{"text": "State Board of Elections\nTimeline of Election Security Activities\n\nSigned contract with Sidus Group, an Anne Arundel County based\ndata center. Sidus Group was (and continues to be) a Master\nContractor under the Maryland Dept. of Information Technology\u2019s\n(DoIT) master contract.\n\nDecember 2014\n\nJanuary 1, 2015 Current contract with Sidus Group for data center hosting begins.\n\nByteGrid LLC purchases Sidus Group. Sidus Group remains the\nname on file with DoIT.\n\nReceive audit of SBE systems hosted by Sidus. Audit covers\nSeptember 2015 October 1, 2014 through June 30, 2015. No reported findings.\n\nUnusual activity on SBE\u2019s online voter registration and ballot\ndelivery system. More information about incident and response.\n\nReceive audit of SBE systems hosted by Sidus. Audit covers July\nSeptember 2016 1, 2015 through June 30, 2016. No reported findings.\n\nIndependent review of data information from the unusual activity.\nThree entities - FBI, State\u2019s cybersecurity vendor, and a third\ncybersecurity firm - came to same conclusion - no evidence of\nbreach or compromise.\n\n. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) starts performing weekly\nOctober 2016 - Present vulnerability scans on SBE websites\n\nAdd additional monitoring and analytics (using artificial\nintelligence) of network traffic to Sidus-hosted systems?\n\nApril 2017 Start monthly process of reviewing all computers at the local\np boards of elections accessing State election systems\nApril 2017 Receive audit of SBE systems hosted by Sidus. Audit covers\np calendar year 2016. No reported findings.\nDHS conducts risk and vulnerability assessment on several critical\nNovember 6 - 17, 2017 election systems. Recommendations made and implemented.\nDHS starts performing assessments of State and local election\n\nNovember 2017 - Present facilities (office and warehouses). As of September 2018, 17\nfacilities have been assessed, and 14 offices have their reports.\n\n2015\n\nAugust 2016\nSeptember - October 2016\n\nJanuary 2017\n\nState (4) and local (1) election officials participate in a national\nDecember 2017 table top exercises hosted by Harvard University\u2019s Belfer Center,\na program of the Kennedy School of Government\n\nFebruary 5 - 6, 2018 Risk and Vulnerability Assessment, External Dependencies and\n\n1 The systems hosted by Sidus are: (1) MDVOTERS; (2) SBE\u2019s suite of online voter services; and (3) unofficial\nresults on election night.",
